(footprint "RP2354A-QFN-60-1EP_7x7mm_P0.4mm_EP-vias"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "kicad-footprint-generator")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "RP2354A / RP2350A QFN-60, 7x7mm, 0.4mm pitch, 3.4x3.4mm exposed pad, with five ground vias through the pad. Pin 61 (the centre pad) is the part's ONLY ground connection, so it carries the entire return current. Forked from KiCad Package_DFN_QFN:QFN-60-1EP_7x7mm_P0.4mm_EP3.4x3.4mm rather than from the stock _ThermalVias variant, because that variant drills 0.2mm (under JLCPCB standard process and under this project's 0.3mm minimum) and its paste apertures overlap the via barrels by 0.31mm. Here the vias are 0.50/0.30mm (0.10mm annular ring, the project minimum) in a plus at 1.2mm, tented on the bottom, ORDINARY plated through holes rather than filled - plugged-via rules exclude a via with a mask opening on either side and the exposed pad is one. Paste is four windows at (+/-0.925, +/-0.925) 1.25x1.25mm: 54.1% coverage, inside IPC-7093A 50-60% band, clearing every barrel by 0.05mm. Specify a 0.12mm stencil.")
	(tags "QFN NoLead RP2354 RP2350 EP vias")
